# DTF tier manifest: s3-copy-length-required
#   artifact-keeper#3737 (PR #4321, 1.11.0): proxy-cache publishes failed on
#   Google Cloud Storage's S3-compatible API because CopyObject was sent
#   without Content-Length and GCS answers 411 Length Required.
#   Profile-set: s3 (MinIO) + storage.s3-copy-411 (new: a pass-through in
#   front of MinIO that answers 411 to exactly that request) +
#   upstreams.mock-static (a counting static upstream for a remote repo).
#
# THE BUG
# A remote repository's proxy cache writes the fetched body to a staging key
# and publishes it to the live key with a server-side copy. On an endpoint
# that requires Content-Length on every PUT, that CopyObject failed with 411
# on every publish: the backend logged "failed to publish staged proxy-cache
# object to the live key; not caching" and refetched the upstream on every
# request. The fix retries a 411-refused CopyObject as a signed CopyObject
# carrying `Content-Length: 0`, and every later copy on that backend sends it
# up front ("S3 endpoint rejected CopyObject without Content-Length (411);
# retrying ... (#3737)"). Since #3916 the generic upload route promotes its
# staged object with the same copy, so it pays the same retry.
#
# Gates: (CONTROL) a generic upload through the shim is 201 and downloads
# byte-exact; the shim is in the backend's S3 path; three GETs through the
# remote all answer the exact upstream bytes (both images). (FIX) those three
# GETs reach the upstream once (cached after the first) and the backend
# logged no failed publish; the shim refused a header-less CopyObject and
# then received CopyObjects carrying Content-Length; a later proxy publish
# goes straight to the Content-Length form (no new 411).
#
# RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED=false: not under test. UPSTREAM_ALLOW_PRIVATE_IPS=true:
# the mock upstream is on a private subnet.
#
# Red: ak-backend:1.10.0. Green: ak-backend:1.11.0 and main.
PROFILES="storage.s3 storage.s3-copy-411 upstreams.mock-static"
ORACLE="oracle.sh"
RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED="false"
UPSTREAM_ALLOW_PRIVATE_IPS="true"
